-- title:
--   Proposition 3.11: Invariant cone membership splits across Jordan components
-- statement:
--   All vector spaces and Lie algebras are finite dimensional and real, with their usual Hausdorff topology. An invariant set is invariant under the group generated by $e^{\operatorname{ad}y}$. A closed convex set is pointed when its recession edge is zero. Write $\mathcal O_x=\operatorname{Inn}(\mathfrak g)x$, $\operatorname{co}(x)=\overline{\operatorname{conv}}\mathcal O_x$, and $C_x=\operatorname{cone}(\mathcal O_x)$. Admissibility means existence of a pointed generating invariant closed convex subset.
--
--   Let $\mathfrak g$ be reductive and $W$ any invariant closed convex cone. Write $x=x_0+x_s+x_n$, with $x_0$ central and $x_s,x_n\in[\mathfrak g,\mathfrak g]$ a commuting ad-semisimple/ad-nilpotent Jordan pair. Then
--
--   $$x\in W\iff x_0+x_s\in W\ \text{and}\ x_n\in W.$$
--
--   No pointedness or generation is assumed, and membership on the left is not assumed in advance. This is the unrestricted equivalence proved by the source.
-- source:
--   Elements in pointed invariant cones in Lie algebras and corresponding affine pairs, arXiv:2110.07297v1, PDF p. 10, Proposition 3.11: Invariant cone membership splits across Jordan components

